cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "FluxCell: a MUSCL-Hancock/HLLC shallow-water solver for WebGPU"
type: software
version: 0.9.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/uihilab/FluxCell"
date-released: 2026-10-21
authors:
  - family-names: "Erazo Ramirez"
    given-names: "Carlos"
    affiliation: "Tulane University"
  - family-names: "Demir"
    given-names: "Ibrahim"
    affiliation: "Tulane University"
keywords:
  - shallow-water equations
  - MUSCL-Hancock
  - HLLC
  - WebGPU
  - WGSL
  - flood modelling
  - finite volume
abstract: >-
  A conservative, well-balanced, second-order finite-volume solver for the 2D shallow-water
  equations (MUSCL-Hancock reconstruction, HLLC fluxes, hydrostatic reconstruction) written as
  WebGPU compute shaders, with wet/dry fronts, Manning friction, rain and point sources, solid
  cells, stage and discharge hydrograph boundaries, a fused single-dispatch tiled kernel with a
  GPU-resident timestep, and f64 CPU references.
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "FluxCell: A Single-Dispatch MUSCL-Hancock Solver for Shallow Flow and Scalar Transport in WebGPU"
